rota lap 4559, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; its DUAL seat is the marked value, whose own text says the amphora's shoulder line names what rides inside, so the lap read the vessel's three fields at the door rather than arguing about them
think Opened cold with standing_equipment_run.sh --detach and held the tree still for its whole 47 minutes; every write until it closed went to amphora/bin/ and .lap/, both gitignored, so tree_at_open equalled tree_at_close.
think Read the earth row's three documents. The dual seat, foundations/20260703-202312_the-marked-value.md, states that every manifest entry carries three fields -- type-mark, digest, name. Two of the three had walls: mark_verdict for the mark, resin_body_proven for the digest. The name had name_verdict, which reads one name's FACE, and nothing anywhere asked whether two lines named one place.
think Every wall in the vessel family reads exactly one cargo line. A duplicate is a relation BETWEEN lines, so no per-line rule can see it. Measured rather than argued: built the CLI, poured a two-file season, opened the seal, rewrote the second cargo line's name to the first's, resealed and restamped.
obs On metal 20260910.090000, before a line changed: the forged vessel answered `listing agrees count=2` at the readable door, carried across a dock whole, and restored through `restore resins proven count=2` and `restore files proven count=2` before refusing on the parent compare -- with the out-home standing, holding one file named a.txt whose bytes were b.txt's. Every digest was honest; only the mapping was not.
obs Three doors welcomed it and the fourth refused after the mutation. That is the shape my own last lap closed one clause over at 20260910.073234: a refusal that arrives after the write is not a wall. The escaping-name rule had been the same reading one field earlier.
obs The rule is published once and borrowed twice, the way the wreck rule and the containment rule already are. A judgment written per caller is a judgment two files may come to disagree about, which manifest_entry.rye's own comment says about the seven readers of parse_manifest_line.
obs The two walls stand in SERIES, and the witness says so rather than implying one path proves both. The listing door refuses first, so the listed plant proves the outer wall alone. The elder vessel shape -- a head with no manifest line, which verify_manifest_agrees answers as no claim rather than as a disagreement -- gives the restore reader its own leg, and it refuses at cargo unproven before restore resins proven is reached. Both walls were removed in turn and the named leg watched to fall.
obs The fetch reader is untouched on purpose: vessel_fetch_delivery.parse_cargo_lines collects digests alone and never reads a name, so a repeated name cannot reach it. Stated rather than assumed -- read at 20260910.
obs The ledger is still full. REDS reads 40,771 of 40,960, 189 bytes, where a row costs near twelve hundred, so this defect is cited by its stamp under the derived-spine law's rule 4 rather than booked.
